  ("How much does AC repair cost in Barrie?", "AC repair cost in Barrie depends on the part that failed, so we quote every repair in writing after diagnosis and before any work. Capacitors, contactors and fan motors are modest repairs; a compressor or evaporator coil on an old unit can approach the price of a new system, and at that point we show you the replacement options, including a cold-climate heat pump from $5,500 installed."),
  ("How fast can you get to an AC repair in Barrie?", "We book Barrie AC repairs seven days a week, with emergency service in the evenings and on holidays when there is no cooling and someone in the home is at risk from heat. We give you a realistic window when you call rather than a promise we can't keep during a heat wave."),
  ("Why won't my air conditioner start after a Barrie winter?", "An air conditioner that won't start after winter most often has a failed run capacitor, a stuck contactor, chewed wiring from rodents or a tripped breaker. Check the breaker and the outdoor disconnect first, then call us. Do not keep trying to start a humming compressor, because that can damage it."),
  ("Should I cover my AC for the winter in Barrie?", "A breathable top cover or a piece of plywood weighted over the fan keeps roof-slide ice and heavy snow out of the fan and fins. Never wrap the whole unit in plastic, because trapped moisture rusts the cabinet and mice love a sealed, dry box. Raising the unit onto a stand does more good than any cover."),
  ("Is it worth repairing a 15-year-old air conditioner in Barrie?", "A capacitor or fan motor on a 15-year-old AC is usually worth fixing. A compressor or major refrigerant leak on a unit that age usually is not, and in Barrie the replacement that makes the most sense is often a cold-climate heat pump, which cools in summer, heats most of the winter and qualifies for a rebate."),
